---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="publish a portfolio project · freestack."
  description="Choose a deployment for a student project, publish a working demo, and make it easy to review."
>
  <section class="ds-wrap py-[88px] sm:py-[110px]">
    <div class="ds-section-label">
      <span class="ds-section-num">04</span>
      <span class="ds-section-name">Student path</span>
      <span class="ds-hairline flex-1"></span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.6rem)] leading-[1.05] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">
      Ship a demo.<br /><span class="text-ink-3">Make your work easy to see.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mb-10 max-w-2xl text-ink-2">
      A deployed project lets someone try it without setting up your code. Pair the demo with a clear project page, source link, and setup notes. Choose hosting for the project you built, not the other way around.
    </p>

    <div class="mb-16 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/catalogs?need=hosting#directory" class="ds-btn ds-btn-filled">compare hosting options <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href="/guides/claim-order" class="ds-btn ds-btn-outline">check student offers</a>
    </div>

    <div class="ds-section-label">
      <span class="ds-section-num">01</span>
      <span class="ds-section-name">Choose a deployment shape</span>
      <span class="ds-hairline flex-1"></span>
    </div>
    <dl class="mb-16 divide-y divide-b1 border-y border-b1">
      <div class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
        <dt class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-ink-3">Static site</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">Portfolio, documentation, or frontend-only demo. Compare build limits, custom domains, and preview deployments. Start with the <a href="/catalogs?need=hosting#directory" class="text-sand underline-offset-2 hover:underline">hosting catalog</a>.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
        <dt class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-ink-3">Full-stack demo</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">A web app with data or sign-in may need separate hosting, database, and auth services. Check sleep behavior and free-tier limits before sharing the demo. Browse <a href="/catalogs?need=databases#directory" class="text-sand underline-offset-2 hover:underline">databases</a> and <a href="/catalogs?need=auth#directory" class="text-sand underline-offset-2 hover:underline">authentication</a>.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-2 py-5 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
        <dt class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] text-ink-3">Always-running backend</dt>
        <dd class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">A worker, bot, or live service needs a host that keeps the process available. Confirm sleep, runtime, and usage caps; a free plan may pause or stop serving when its limits are reached.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <div class="ds-section-label">
      <span class="ds-section-num">02</span>
      <span class="ds-section-name">Make the project reviewable</span>
      <span class="ds-hairline flex-1"></span>
    </div>
    <p class="mb-6 max-w-xl text-ink-2">Give a visitor enough context to understand and try the work quickly.</p>
    <ul class="mb-12 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-3 border-y border-b1 py-6 text-[0.95rem] text-ink-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <li>What problem it solves and who it is for</li>
      <li>Your role and the parts you built</li>
      <li>A screenshot or short demo video</li>
      <li>A working demo link and source repository</li>
      <li>Setup instructions and a short stack summary</li>
      <li>What you learned or would improve next</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-16 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-ink-3">
      GitHub suggests highlighting a small set of relevant projects, writing useful READMEs, and linking demos or project sites from your profile. A custom domain is optional; add one after the demo works reliably.
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/account-and-profile/tutorials/using-your-github-profile-to-enhance-your-resume" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sand underline-offset-2 hover:underline">Read GitHub’s profile guide ↗</a>
    </p>

    <div class="border-t border-b1 pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Before you share it</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-ink-2">Check whether the host allows your intended use, whether the demo sleeps, and what happens at the usage limit. Student offers require eligibility and may have separate terms. Re-check the provider’s current terms before relying on an offer.</p>
      <a href="/catalogs?need=hosting#directory" class="mt-5 inline-flex text-sm text-sand underline-offset-2 hover:underline">Compare hosting limits and terms →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
